17:["$","p","1",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"The medical record serves clinical care first, but it is also a legal document, the basis for billing, and the evidence in any dispute. Everything you enter carries your name and a timestamp, and it is permanent."}]
18:["$","figure","2",{"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200","children":["$","table",null,{"className":"w-full text-left border-collapse","children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"className":"bg-gray-50","children":[["$","th","0",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"Write this"}],["$","th","1",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"Not this"}],["$","th","2",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"Because"}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","0",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"\"Patient reports pain 8/10 in right lower abdomen\""}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"\"Patient in severe pain\""}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Severity is the patient's report, quantified — not your assessment"}]]}],["$","tr","1",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"\"BP 158/96, right arm, seated, large cuff\""}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"\"BP high\""}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"High is an interpretation; the number and conditions are the fact"}]]}],["$","tr","2",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"\"Patient states 'I stopped taking it two weeks ago'\""}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"\"Patient is non-compliant\""}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Non-compliant is a judgment, and it prejudices everyone who reads it afterwards"}]]}],["$","tr","3",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"\"Patient declined the injection\""}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"\"Patient refused and was difficult\""}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Declining is a fact; difficult is an opinion with no clinical value"}]]}],["$","tr","4",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"\"Wound 3 cm, edges approximated, no drainage\""}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"\"Wound looks fine\""}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Measured description is reproducible; fine is not"}]]}]]}]]}]}],["$","figcaption",null,{"className":"text-sm text-gray-500 mt-2 italic","children":"Objective and subjective"}]]}]
19:["$","div","3",{"className":"p-4 rounded-xl border-l-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed bg-yellow-50 border-yellow-400","children":[false,"Never document an assessment, an interpretation, or a diagnosis. Recording 'appears dehydrated' or 'probably a virus' is clinical judgment, which is outside an MA's scope, and it may steer a provider who reads it before seeing the patient. Record what you measured, what you observed physically, and what the patient told you."]}]
1a:["$","p","4",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"Errors are corrected, never erased. In a paper record, draw a single line through the error so it remains readable, write the correction, and initial and date it. In an EHR, use the amendment function — which preserves the original entry and records who changed what and when. Deleting or overwriting an entry destroys the audit trail and looks, in litigation, exactly like concealment."}]
1b:["$","div","5",{"className":"p-4 rounded-xl border-l-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed bg-yellow-50 border-yellow-400","children":[false,"Never document in advance, and never document care you did not personally provide or witness. Charting a vital sign before you take it, or signing for a colleague's work, is falsification of a medical record — a serious offence independent of whether anything went wrong. It is also one of the fastest ways to lose a healthcare career."]}]
1c:["$","$L20","6",{"block":{"type":"knowledge-check","question":"You realize you entered a vital sign in the wrong patient's chart an hour ago. What should you do?","options":["Delete the entry so the wrong record is not affected","Use the EHR's amendment or correction function, which preserves the original entry and records the change","Leave it and add a note to the correct chart","Ask a colleague to remove it under their login"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"Corrections must preserve the audit trail. The amendment function marks the entry as corrected while retaining the original and recording who changed it and when. Deletion destroys the evidence that the error occurred and was addressed, which is far worse than the error itself.","optionRationales":["Deleting destroys the audit trail and, in litigation, is indistinguishable from concealing an error.","Correct. Amend it so the original, the correction, and the author are all preserved.","The wrong chart still contains incorrect clinical data, which could affect that patient's care.","Using another person's login is a serious violation on its own, quite apart from the documentation issue."]}}]
1d:["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-12","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3","children":"Challenge"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl","children":"Apply what you've learned in this lesson."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-md border border-gray-200 p-8","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"Documentation quality is a habit built one entry at a time."}],["$","ol","1",{"start":"$undefined","className":"list-decimal pl-6 space-y-3 text-gray-700 marker:font-semibold marker:text-primary-600","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Rewrite each objectively: 'Patient was rude and uncooperative.' 'Vitals look okay.' 'Patient seems to be getting worse.' 'Wound is healing nicely.'"}],["$","li","1",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Research the SOAP note format. Identify which sections an MA would typically contribute to and which belong to the provider."}],["$","li","2",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Write a complete intake entry for a patient presenting with a cough, using only objective language and quoting the chief complaint."}],["$","li","3",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Find out how your EHR — or any EHR you can research — handles amendments. Describe what the audit trail preserves."}]]}]]}]}]]}]
